          "input_json": "{\u0022path\u0022:\u0022concepts/retrieval-patterns.md\u0022,\u0022content\u0022:\u0022---\\ntype: Concept\\ntitle: Retrieval Patterns\\ndescription: Techniques for combining and ranking results from multiple retrieval methods, with emphasis on hybrid retrieval combining lexical and vector search.\\ntimestamp: 2026-07-14T00:00:00Z\\ntags:\\n  - concept/Retrieval\\n  - concept/Ranking\\n  - concept/RAG\\nconfidence: medium\\nconfidence_reason: \\u0022Two sources; practical adoption confirmed in production systems.\\u0022\\n---\\n\\n## Hybrid Retrieval\\n\\nHybrid retrieval combines sparse lexical search (e.g. BM25) with dense vector search, then merges the two ranked result sets, often via reciprocal rank fusion. This approach captures both exact term matches and semantic similarity.\\n\\nHybrid retrieval consistently outperforms either method alone on queries mixing rare identifiers (error codes, product SKUs) with natural language intent. It has become the default retrieval pattern in production RAG systems.\\n\\n## Ranking Strategies\\n\\nUse reciprocal rank fusion for robust merging of multiple ranked result sets.\\n\\n## Citations\\n\\n[^1]: Hybrid retrieval definition and production adoption pattern, unnamed technical source.\\n\u0022}"
